    "result_text": "Done. The full suite is green (10 tests, 0 failures), and the new `AcceptanceTest.coreRiskFlagFalseNormally` passes.\n\n## What I implemented\n\n`riskFlag` is an OR of the three markers in the spec, all derivable from an owner's already-stored/derived state, so it's computed once at response time and is identical whether the owner is read via `POST /api/owners` or `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `riskFlag` boolean to the `Owner` schema (the DTO is generated from here; `OwnerDto.riskFlag` is generated with `@JsonProperty` and no `NON_NULL`, so a `false` value is serialized, which the test asserts).\n\n2. **`DisposableEmailDomains`** \u2014 added `isDisposableAdjacent(domain)`: not itself blocked, but shares a registrable label (`mailinator`, `tempmail`, `guerrillamail`) with a known disposable provider \u2014 covering different-TLD (`mailinator.net`) and subdomain (`smtp.mailinator.com`) cases. The label set is derived from the existing blocklist, so there's one source of truth. This sits with the existing disposable-domain knowledge rather than being copied.\n\n3. **`RiskFlag`** (new util) \u2014 `RiskFlag.of(owner)` = `possibleDuplicate` OR `capacityWarning` (the stored \"city over soft capacity 40\u201349 at creation\" marker) OR disposable-adjacent email domain. Null-safe, single responsibility, mirroring the other derived-value utils (`OwnerSegment`, `MembershipPoints`).\n\n4. **`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 a `riskFlag(owner)` mapping expression delegating to `RiskFlag.of`, alongside the other derived-field mappings.\n\nNo new DB column or pipeline step was needed: two of the three inputs are already persisted flags and the third is a pure lookup on the stored email, so deriving `riskFlag` in the mapper reuses existing logic and stays consistent across both endpoints.",
